            </profile>
            <profile id="3843-7197-5c5a-fb7f" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword. May have shield (+2), light armour (+3), javelins (+2), throwing spear (+4). May be mounted on a horse (M7, +8). If on foot, may have a large shield (+3). Army General. Up to two Character Advantages from the composition. Character Advantages: up to two for an Army General, one for any other character only if the army list allows it. Each advantage may be taken once per 1,000 points (or part thereof) in the army and once per character (not enforced). (The Age of Arthur p.26)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="aa22-27a4-c559-a0cc" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
