  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6405-3367-a183-e627" name="Romano-British Civitates: Twilight of Britannia and Brittany (Age of Arthur) - List Notes" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false">
      <description>ROMANO-BRITISH CIVITATES: TWILIGHT OF BRITANNIA AND BRITTANY (The Age of Arthur, pp.21-31). Units of Commanipulares, Milites (including Sagittari and Equites) and Pedyt may have a Leader (+5), Musician (+5) and Standard (+5). Allies are documented only. Special rules in the book: Allies, Christian Priest, Shieldwall, Light Troops, Character Advantages.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Romano-British Civitates - Twilight of Britannia]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 20%
  TWILIGHT OF BRITANNIA (c.410-450). Characters up to 33% (led by a Dux/Comes, Magnate or a Tribune upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Commanipulares, Milites incl. Sagittari and Equites, Pedyt). Uncommon up to 20% (Rustici). Allies up to 33% from one list: Franks (Early Merovingian: Franci led by 0-1 Dux or Antrustio) or Saxons (Sea Raiders: Geoguth led by 0-1 Atheling or Thegn). Advantages: Born to the Purple, Fabricae, Fearsome Blow, Finest Armour, Finest Horses, Knight Commander, Loyalty, Man of the People, Professional, Veteran.
[Romano-British Civitates - Brittany]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 20%
  BRITTANY. Characters up to 33% (Dux/Comes or a Tribune upgraded to Army General; no Magnate). Common warriors at least 33% (Commanipulares, Milites incl. Sagittari and Equites, Pedyt). Uncommon up to 20% (Rustici). Allies up to 25% from one list: Franks (Early Merovingian) or Saxons (Sea Raiders). If the army includes a Dux/Comes it must also include a Bishop. Advantages: Boats, Fearsome Blow, Finest Armour, Finest Horses, Knight Commander, Loyalty, Mounted Raider, Professional, Veteran.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
